These are the few that I am aware of:

1. The full moon bug:  Saving on a full moon always decreases luck
by 1.  Unfortunately, even though a character created on a full
moon starts with a luck of +1, restoring a saved one on a full moon
doesn't get any bonus luck.  Therefore, restoring any character on
a full moon (whether it was created on a full moon or not) and then
saving it causes luck to decrease, just for saving it alone.

2. Elves are not generated with elven stuff (weapon and armor) as
intended.

3. Exploding a bag on the ground (by #looting instead of applying
it) causes dungeon collapse.

4. Blessing (or cursing) a (non-empty) bag of holding doesn't
properly adjust the weight of the bag.

5. Some other possibly Macintosh-specific bug I can't remember.

